{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380949-v5-extent-of-the-lasombra-bane","id":1380949,"title":"V5 extent of the lasombra bane?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-13T07:59:32-07:00","id":1380949,"title":"V5 extent of the lasombra bane?","content":"The book is somewhat vague on the extent of the curse and I want to be sure I understand it.<br /> So from what I read it mainly applies to technologies that need to record, transmit or detect the presence of the user in some way (touch screens, video/voice recordings, motion sensors, voice activation, fingerprint scanners etc and this also applies to natural occurrences such as reflections in water or not always having an echo in caves.<br /> So more simple technology wouldn't trigger their bane such as elevator buttons, texting on older cellphones that dont use a touchscreen, desktop PC using keyboard and mouse, driving a car etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","name":"Syren1987","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:10:01-07:00","id":1380988,"title":"","content":"Texting on old cell phones would still count, it's &quot;any kind of communicative technology.&quot; Desktop PC I think would be a bizarre gray area where they could write a Word document just fine but have a hard time writing an email.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:42:57-07:00","id":1380999,"title":"","content":"Rereading the content in Chicago by night it says &quot;similarly, modern technology relying on touch or other forms of direct interaction -- such as voice activation or use of a stylus -- tends to glitch or simply act unresponsive&quot;. Don't see anything about all communication technology. Which I dont understand the in universe logic for how that would even work. I understand touch screens and styluses as both depend on the user's electrical current to detect interaction. This is why touchscreens dont work if your wearing gloves etc. All communication technologies goes down a pretty deep rabbit hole of what constitutes technology; telegraphs, sending Morse code with a flashlight? And if their bane was that debilitating wouldn't simple tech like light switches fall under the shadow of their bane. Feel like they really should of spent a few more sentences detailing it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","user":"Syren1987","date":". 04-13-2020, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","name":"Syren1987","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:58:16-07:00","id":1381050,"title":"","content":"The &quot;modern communication technology&quot; quote is in the next paragraph and goes onto say &quot;including making a simple phone call, requires a Technology test at Difficulty 2 + Bane Severity as microphones have similar problems with the voice of a Lasombra as cameras with their image&quot;. Out of context, that doesn't necessarily mean <i>all</i> modern communication technology and that particular example doesn't give any reason for why they couldn't send a text message using a phone with buttons. I note that a phone call is a lot less modern than an email, let alone SMS.<br /> <br /> If Lasombra can use keyboards without difficulty, it's not<i> that</i> significant: you just text people on a \u00a320 phone and if you must make a live phonecall from your haven, text-to-voice softwareusing a PC and peripheral speaker. You can't conviently use smartphone functions without a laptop and emulator, but how much does that rule out? Whereas no telecommunications in general would affect gameplay more substantially, but I don't see that as an extension of not casting reflections and such. I think that typing is more akin to writing or painting an image of your choice than transmitting a visual or audio image of yourself. Unless the problem is with the transmission or reception rather than the capture of the input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 04-13-2020, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T13:02:05-07:00","id":1381069,"title":"","content":"So what your saying is rather than technology just having trouble registering that the lasombra is present; it's more that technology malfunctions to direct interaction from the lasombra?<br /> This would make sense as the book mentions lasombra using drivers rather than operating vehicles themselves and i can't see that being necessary unless the latter was true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","name":"Syren1987","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T13:37:25-07:00","id":1381081,"title":"","content":"The book is annoyingly unclear about this and contradicts itself in different places, but one of the writers has clarified the intent behind it: it's meant to affect technology that detects or responds to the user's presence directly, like a camera (sensing your image), a microphone (sensing your voice), or a touchscreen (sensing your capacitance). Mechanical keyboards, steering wheels, and elevator buttons are unaffected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:02:46-07:00","id":1381086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380949-v5-extent-of-the-lasombra-bane?p=1381081#post1381081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book is annoyingly unclear about this and contradicts itself in different places, but one of the writers has clarified the intent behind it: it's meant to affect technology that detects or responds to the user's presence directly, like a camera (sensing your image), a microphone (sensing your voice), or a touchscreen (sensing your capacitance). Mechanical keyboards, steering wheels, and elevator buttons are unaffected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks; I thought that was what they were going for but wasn't sure. Was unsure because of a few passages in the book and the fact it seems as it may be to easy to work around the bane. Then again Ventrue could just run a night club that caters to their taste etc. so the bane probably causes problems when they are out and about rather than when they are holed up in their haven where they would likely setup workarounds to make their bane more manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","name":"Syren1987","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:48:12-07:00","id":1381103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380949-v5-extent-of-the-lasombra-bane?p=1381081#post1381081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book is annoyingly unclear about this and contradicts itself in different places, but one of the writers has clarified the intent behind it: it's meant to affect technology that detects or responds to the user's presence directly, like a camera (sensing your image), a microphone (sensing your voice), or a touchscreen (sensing your capacitance). Mechanical keyboards, steering wheels, and elevator buttons are unaffected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a source cited for that writer clarification? I'd like to see/hear the wording they use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:52:08-07:00","id":1381105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380949-v5-extent-of-the-lasombra-bane?p=1381081#post1381081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book is annoyingly unclear about this and contradicts itself in different places, but one of the writers has clarified the intent behind it: it's meant to affect technology that detects or responds to the user's presence directly, like a camera (sensing your image), a microphone (sensing your voice), or a touchscreen (sensing your capacitance). Mechanical keyboards, steering wheels, and elevator buttons are unaffected.</div> </div> </div> </div>so basically: if you could operate it with a long stick a lasombra could use it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:52:20-07:00","id":1381106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380949-v5-extent-of-the-lasombra-bane?p=1381081#post1381081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book is annoyingly unclear about this and contradicts itself in different places, but one of the writers has clarified the intent behind it: it's meant to affect technology that detects or responds to the user's presence directly, like a camera (sensing your image), a microphone (sensing your voice), or a touchscreen (sensing your capacitance). Mechanical keyboards, steering wheels, and elevator buttons are unaffected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, until they get very old anyway... I have no problem with seeing this as a progressive deterioration, explaining why the truly ancient of the line dwell in the oceanic abysses or never emerge from shadow form etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T15:13:25-07:00","id":1381112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380949-v5-extent-of-the-lasombra-bane?p=1381103#post1381103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a source cited for that writer clarification? I'd like to see/hear the wording they use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't seem to make an image embed, but <a href=\"https://discordapp.com/channels/478848548247568384/478887731632668683/554761485033668639\" target=\"_blank\">here's a direct link to the message on the V5 Discord server</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T16:01:56-07:00","id":1381125,"title":"","content":"For those who'd rather not go thru the trouble of opening discord this is the relevant conversation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#F1C40F\">Sharkey</span>03/11/2019<br /> I feel that saying Keyboards work would open the door to &quot;Yeah just use a stylus and text then you can have your phone back&quot;<br /> I suppose we could, yeah.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C40000\">Ryn</span>03/11/2019<br /> Touchscreen glitches...<br /> a keyboard isn't a microphone I dunno it's a good question.<br /> Someone ask....<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#F1C40F\">Sharkey</span>03/11/2019<br /> @Matthew Dawkins, if you're free and don't mind answering a question for us- how do you feel about the Lasombra bane and keyboards? It's pretty clear about touch screens, microphones, and the like- but I am personally unsure if a keyboard and mouse would fall under 'direct interaction', though leaning towards 'yes'. Thanks for your time, and the wonderful product that is Chicago by Night!<br /> <br /> Matthew Dawkins03/11/2019<br /> I would actually be fine with that. They can also still drive cars if they want. I'll be making a clearer distinction once the book is done in editing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C40000\">Generalissimo</span>03/11/2019<br /> Aren't modern cars FILLED with the stuff?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C40000\">Ashe (She/They)</span>03/11/2019<br /> I think the intention is that the Lasombra are hard to detect, meaning a touchscreen would have a hard time picking them up, but a mechanical keyboard for example is just detecting buttons being pushed rather than the lasombra itself<br /> It has a degree of seperation<br /> Same with a car, the lasombra isn't being detected, merely the actions the lasombra performs<br /> If it has a fancy touchscreen stereo it might have some trouble, but pressing a peddle is pressing a peddle no matter how much you don't show up in mirrors<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C40000\">storyncode</span>03/11/2019<br /> That\u2019s the way I\u2019d go through the logic. If it\u2019s based on direct contact with the kindred, issues, if it\u2019s something that\u2019s not a direct interaction (non-touch based keyboard) no issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","user":"Syren1987","date":". 04-13-2020, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","name":"Syren1987","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}